  2006	  Lenstra--Pomerance algorithm on integers $\le\sqrt{2N}$, and at most $2k$ special-$q$ searches. The first has expected cost
  2007	  $L_{\sqrt{2N}}[1/2,1+o(1)]=L^{1/\sqrt2+o(1)}$ (Fact~\ref{fact:LP}), uniformly over the inputs. Each search costs $\tilde O(B+S^2\log N)=L^{1/\sqrt2+o(1)}$
