   316	in time $L_{\sqrt N}[1/2,1+o(1)]=L_N[1/2,1/\sqrt2+o(1)]$, and that is exactly where the constant $1/\sqrt2$
   317	comes from. Any improvement of the rigorous constant for factoring $\sqrt N$-size integers would
   318	improve ours (Section~\ref{sec:limits}).
