  2231	\begin{corollary}[portfolio; ``Corollary P'']\label{cor:P}
  2232	There is a single Las Vegas algorithm that outputs the complete factorisation of every $N\ge2$ in expected time $L_N[1/2,o(1)]$, that is,
  2233	$\exp\bigl(o(\sqrt{\log N\log\log N})\bigr)$. No effective rate for the $o(1)$ is supplied. Likewise, running the same schedule over $k$ at
  2234	fixed $d=9$, without recursion, gives a single algorithm with expected time $L_N[1/2,0.9192\ldots+o(1)]$.
  2235	\end{corollary}
  2236	
  2237	\begin{proof}
