  2239	$d_j=2j+7$, $k_j=\lceil d_j^2/4\rceil+j$, $\mu_j$ the (rational) optimum of Lemma~\ref{lem:optmu}, $\eta_{0,j}:=1/d_j^2$, and $a_j$ rational with
  2240	$|a_j-a^*_j|\to0$. These tuples are admissible for every $j$ (the inequalities are monotone in $j$; checked exactly for $j\le60$, where
  2241	$c^*=0.239$ at $j=60$). The slack must tend to $0$, since $\theta\ge\eta_0$. The map $j\mapsto A_j$ is computable. No threshold $N_0(j)$ enters
  2242	the algorithms, because each $A_j$ races its core against trial division at every node (step~3 of Algorithm~\ref{alg:factor}); so
  2243	$N_0(j)$ need not be computable. Let $T_j(N)$ be the running time of $A_j$ on $N$.
  2244	
  2245	\emph{Restart schedule.} In phase $s=1,2,\dots$, run $A_i$ for each $i\le s$, from scratch with fresh coins, for at most $2^{s-i}$ steps.
  2246	Stop at the first certified output. Phase $s$ costs at most $2^s$ steps, up to a polylogarithmic bookkeeping factor.
  2247	
  2248	\emph{Bound.} Fix $j$ and put $s_0:=j+\lceil\log_2(2\Ex T_j(N))\rceil$. In each phase $s\ge s_0$, the run of $A_j$ fails to finish within
  2249	$2^{s-j}\ge2^{s-s_0}\cdot2\Ex T_j$ steps with probability at most $2^{-(s-s_0)-1}$, by Markov. Runs in different phases are independent. So the expected
  2250	time is at most a polylogarithmic factor times
  2251	\[
  2252	2^{s_0+1}+\sum_{m\ge1}2^{s_0+m}2^{-m(m+1)/2}=O\bigl(2^j\,\Ex T_j(N)\bigr).
  2253	\]
